abstract: Zhi bing liang yan (治病良言), printed by the Anglo-Chinese College in Hong
  Kong in 1849, closes with the institutional signature 黃泥涌仁施醫館; its individual author
  is unknown. The tract presents its Christian charitable purpose and account of free
  care, addresses medical expense and encourages early attendance, offering evidence
  for studying medical charity, hospital–patient relations, discourse on expense and
  missionary printing in nineteenth-century Hong Kong. Version 0.2.1 transcribes 12
  original-print text faces across ten images of Bodleian Sinica 1411, providing TXT,
  JSON and TEI XML with references to the official source images. The text is a provisional
  AI transcription without human double collation or expert review. This revision
  applies 1 source-supported character correction following targeted non-blind review
  of reader proposals; it is not a new full-book independent collation.
